monitor/ng	_tp_out=$(api -X GET "/repos/$target/issues/$issue" --jq '.number' 2>&1) || _tp_rc=$?	1	api	absorbed:api->exit	safe	safe -- the CALL SITE CONSUMES THE STATUS, which is the property this manifest asks about. `api` can terminate via `_t=$(token) || exit 1`; inside `$( )` that exits the SUBSHELL, and the `|| _tp_rc=$?` on the very next token captures it. The branch below reads `_tp_rc != 0` together with the TEXT: only a positive 404 refuses, and a token failure -- which is what an `api` termination looks like here -- falls to the WARNING arm and PROCEEDS. That is the intended direction for your-org/nexus-code#1491's pre-flight: a probe that could not LOOK must not block a hand-off it has no finding against, and the upload one step later fails loudly on the same missing token. Note the asymmetry this file records: monitor/ng carries only `set -uo pipefail`, so an UNCONSUMED status here would be a defect -- this row is safe because the status is read on the next line, not because the file is protected.
